    "points": 4,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Consider the following pattern: 1st row: $1$; 2nd row: $1,\\ 3$; 3rd row: $1,\\ 3,\\ 5$; and so on (the rows are the odd numbers $1,3,5,\\dots$). The difference between the sums of the numbers in the $9^{\\text{th}}$ and $10^{\\text{th}}$ rows is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$17$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$18$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$19$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$21$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$22$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Sum of odd numbers",
        "body": "Row $n$ is $1+3+\\dots+(2n-1)=n^2$ (check: $1,4,9$). So the sums are $9^2=81$ and $10^2=100$, with difference $19$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 19**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Compare directly",
        "body": "The $10$th row is the $9$th row with one more number added, namely the tenth odd number $2\\times10-1=19$. So the difference is $19$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 19**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "patterns",
      "sequences-series"
    ],
    "difficulty": 1,
