    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The measurement of $\\angle A$ is (in the figure $AB=AC$, and the point $P$ inside the triangle has $PB=PC$, $\\angle ABP=30^\\circ$ and $\\angle BPC=100^\\circ$)",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2003-r2/q06.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$30^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$40^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$50^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$60^\\circ$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$70^\\circ$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Angle chase",
        "body": "Triangle $PBC$ has $PB=PC$ (one tick each) and apex angle $100^\\circ$, so $\\angle PBC=\\angle PCB=\\frac{180^\\circ-100^\\circ}2=40^\\circ$.\n\nThen $\\angle ABC=\\angle ABP+\\angle PBC=30^\\circ+40^\\circ=70^\\circ$. Since $AB=AC$, $\\angle ACB=70^\\circ$ too, so $\\angle A=180^\\circ-70^\\circ-70^\\circ=40^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $40^\\circ$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "geometry"
    ],
