        "text": "$\\frac12$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$\\frac11$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Triangle areas",
        "body": "The large triangle has base from $0$ to $10$ and height $6$: area $\\frac12\\cdot10\\cdot6=30$. The small triangle has base from $2$ to $8$ and height $2$: area $\\frac12\\cdot6\\cdot2=6$.\n\nThe two A regions are the halves of the small triangle: each has area $3$. The two B regions share the remaining $30-6=24$: each has area $12$.\n\nRatio $\\frac{3}{12}=\\frac14$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac14$**"
      }
    ],
