    "prompt": "$\\triangle ABC$ has $D$ on $BC$ such that $BD=2$ and $DC=3$ (with the right angle at $C$). If $AB=m$ and $AD=n$ then the value of $m^2-n^2$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2003-r2/q11.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$4$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$9$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$16$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$25$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$36$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Pythagoras twice",
        "body": "Let $AC=h$. In right triangle $ACD$: $n^2=h^2+3^2$. In right triangle $ACB$: $m^2=h^2+5^2$ (as $BC=2+3=5$).\n\nSubtract: $m^2-n^2=25-9=16$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 16**"
      }
    ],
