        "title": "Count factors of 5",
        "body": "Each trailing zero needs a factor $2\\times5$; there are far more factors of $2$ than of $5$, so count the factors of $5$ in $200!$: $\\lfloor200/5\\rfloor+\\lfloor200/25\\rfloor+\\lfloor200/125\\rfloor=40+8+1=49$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 49**"
