    "prompt": "A tank that is in the form of an inverted cone contains a liquid. The height $h$, in metres, of the space above the liquid is given by the formula $h=21-\\frac72r$ where $r$ is the radius of the liquid surface, in metres. The circumference of the top of the tank, in metres is",
