    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Speed ratio",
        "body": "In the first race Petrus runs $90$ m while Lee is beaten by $4$ m, i.e. Lee has run $96$ m in the same time. So Lee's speed : Petrus's speed $=96:90=16:15$.\n\nFor a dead heat Lee runs $100$ m while Petrus runs $100\\times\\frac{15}{16}=93.75$ m, so Petrus gets a lead of $100-93.75=6.25$ m.\n\n**Answer: (D) 6.25 m**"
