      {
        "title": "Column sums",
        "body": "The sum is $100(T+P+R)+10\\cdot3S+(R+R+P)=100(T+P+R)+30S+2R+P$. Since $T+S+R+P=17$, $T+P+R=17-S$, so the sum is $1700-70S+2R+P$.\n\nTo make it large we want $S$ as small as possible: $S=2$, then give the largest digit to $R$ and next to $P$: $R=7$, $P=5$ (and $T=3$): the sum is $1700-140+14+5=1579$. (Check: $327+527+725=1579$.)\n\nAny larger $S$ loses at least $70$, while the term $2R+P$ ranges only between $2\\cdot3+5=11$ and $2\\cdot7+5=19$ (at most $8$ of a difference), so $S=2$ is best.\n\n**Answer: (A) 1579**"
